    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26737" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnyphus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĭf-</span></b> ),
			i, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnyphĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĭf-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnyphĭārĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">līnĭf-</span></b> ), ĭi,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λινόϋφος,
		λινοϋφής</span> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λι:νυφος</span>, Gloss.),
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
			linen-weaver</i> (post-class.): Scythopolitani linyphi, Cod. Th.
			10, 20, 8: alii linyphiones sunt, Hadr. in Ep. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Vop. Sat. 8</span></i>: corpus
			linyphiariorum, Cod. Th. 10, 20, 16.</div>
